# Version Management Rule

## CRITICAL: Always Update Version

Every time you make changes to this MultiGender Hebrew Text Designer project, you MUST update the version number in both locations:

### 1. JavaScript CONFIG Object
Update the version in [src/script.js](mdc:src/script.js) at line ~11:
```javascript
const CONFIG = {
    VERSION: '1.14.2',  // ← ALWAYS UPDATE THIS
    // ... rest of config
};
```

### 2. HTML Footer Display
Update the version in [src/index.html](mdc:src/index.html) in the footer section:
```html
<span class="version-small">v1.14.2</span>  <!-- ← ALWAYS UPDATE THIS -->
```

## Version Increment Rules

Follow semantic versioning (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH):

- **PATCH** (+0.0.1): Bug fixes, small improvements, CSS tweaks, minor text changes
- **MINOR** (+0.1.0): New features, UI improvements, significant functionality additions  
- **MAJOR** (+1.0.0): Breaking changes, complete rewrites, major architecture changes

## Commit Message Format

Always include version change in commit messages:
```
[Type]: Brief description

- Change 1
- Change 2
- Version: v{old} → v{new}
```

## Files That Require Version Updates

- [src/script.js](mdc:src/script.js) - CONFIG.VERSION
- [src/index.html](mdc:src/index.html) - Footer version display

## Never Forget

- Version updates are MANDATORY for every change
- Both locations must be updated simultaneously
- Include version change in commit message
- Follow semantic versioning principles